{
 "esm": "0.8.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "ISRM_clean",
  "description": "FULLY-AUTOMATIC clean full-domain InMAP ISRM (Phase 5 target). Full-domain SR[src_cells,rcv_cells], E as the emission->cell binning +-aggregate, X/Y as an in-model Lambert-conformal PROJECTION observed over raw emis_lon/emis_lat (the inline trig IS the lambert_conformal_forward_x/y expansion), projected at BUILD time by the general-eval coordinate path (Phase 5 Part A). NO hand-authored pushdown constructs (no derived set / producer / gated_select / member_factor) and NO caller-supplied projected coordinates. Builds with pushdown_rewrite=true: the auto-rewrite (Phase 4) generates the support set + distinct producer + member_factor + gated_select; the gated SR provider is fetched pre-sliced to the invented source cells. NO runner pre-pass. (Not full-scale-validated: Wall #2 type-instability in the observed evaluator is separate/pre-existing; L1-scale machine precision is the Phase-5 acceptance.)",
  "authors": [
   "EarthSciML"
  ],
  "license": "MIT",
  "created": "2026-07-19T00:00:00Z",
  "tags": [
   "isrm",
   "inmap",
   "source_receptor",
   "air_quality",
   "pm25",
   "health_impact",
   "emissions",
   "ff10",
   "nei2016",
   "zarr",
   "lambert_conformal",
   "reprojection",
   "data_loader",
   "variable_map",
   "referenced-component"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Tessum, C.W., Hill, J.D., Marshall, J.D. (2017). InMAP: A model for air pollution interventions. PLoS ONE 12(4): e0176131.",
    "doi": "10.1371/journal.pone.0176131"
   },
   {
    "citation": "InMAP ISRM tutorial (2022-12-15).",
    "url": "https://inmap.run/blog/2022/12/15/tutorial/"
   }
  ],
  "x_esd": {
   "note": "Two-stage runner-orchestrated pipeline (see wave3 design decisions). Stage 1 (runner): ff10 EGU ingest -> LCC project + rectangle spatial join -> ppl (unique emission-bearing source cells) + compact E_p; bind zarr SR provider with lazy select ([0], ppl, :). Stage 2: static evaluation of the observeds below. Expected national totals: ~7,525 deaths (Krewski) / ~16,979 deaths (Lepeule).",
   "phase2_pushdown_DRAFT": {
    "summary": "DRAFT projection-pushdown variant of isrm.esm. The runner pre-pass that computed `ppl` (the distinct emission-bearing source cells) is replaced by an in-.esm value-invention producer aggregate `emis_src_cells_faq` (kind:derived index set emis_src_cells). This document will NOT validate or build until Phase-2-core lands the engine support listed below; it is authored as correct as the schema allows and modelled on tests/valid/geometry/bin_skolem_spatial_join.esm + conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm.",
    "requires_phase2_core": {
     "lcc_at_build_time": "The overlap-gate producer reads the LCC-PROJECTED emission coords X/Y (and the full-grid cell rectangles W/S/E/N) as build-time const factors (index(X,r)/index(Y,r)/index(W,c).. must resolve in materialize_value_invention's const_arrays, value_invention.jl:388). Today the ONLY build-time path into those const_arrays is (a) caller-supplied kwd[:const_arrays] (build.jl:2469) and (b) _derive_binning_coords (build.jl:2476), which materialises via _materialize_geom_array -> _geo_compile, the LIMITED geometry vocabulary that EXCLUDES trig/exp/log/fn/apply_expression_template (geometry_setup.jl:588-604,630-639). X/Y are lambert_conformal_forward_x/y (an apply_expression_template that expands to trig), so _derive_binning_coords cannot evaluate them; _vi_eval has no trig either (value_invention.jl:327-362). The general-eval materialiser _materialize_setup_general_map (geometry_setup.jl:649-662) DOES speak trig/fn via _eval_cellwise but runs inside build_evaluator (build.jl:1350/1388) AFTER materialize_value_invention (build.jl:2485), so its output never reaches value-invention. SMALLEST FIX: route _derive_binning_coords' seed materialisation (geometry_setup.jl:1247) through _materialize_setup_general_map when _body_needs_general_eval(e), threading the model's registered_functions in; then a vi-index-target coordinate observed whose body is the LCC fn/template is evaluated at build time and fed to value-invention. ALTERNATIVE (works today, no engine change): the caller supplies X and Y (and the full-grid cell rectangles W/S/E/N) as const_arrays; the runner still does the cheap per-record LCC projection but the engine does the expensive spatial-join + distinct that invents ppl.",
     "members_fed_back_as_factor": "The producer's vi.members (the invented full-grid source-cell ids, materialize_value_invention's `members` return, value_invention.jl:948-950) must be fed back into the const-array factor `src_cell_of_ppl` (shape [emis_src_cells]) so cell_W/S/E/N = index(W, index(src_cell_of_ppl, c)) can gather the compact rectangles. Today materialize_value_invention returns members/extents but nothing wires members into a named model factor; Phase-2-core must bind vi.members[emis_src_cells_faq] -> const_arrays[\"src_cell_of_ppl\"] before build_evaluator consumes the model.",
     "gated_provider_deferral": "data_loaders.ISRM_SR.gated_select gates the SR source axis by the DERIVED set emis_src_cells (see that loader). The provider load must be DEFERRED until value-invention has materialised emis_src_cells (extent + member order), then deliver SR pre-sliced to the compact [emis_src_cells, rcv_cells] slab. Replaces the runner's lazy_select ([0], ppl, :) (G2). No engine field consumes gated_select today."
    }
   },
   "format_gaps": {
    "G1": "0.8.0 source schema has no `format` field / no .zarray pinning; recorded in loader x_esd.",
    "G2": "No lazy source-dim selection in-format. PUSHDOWN DRAFT: the runner-mediated SR[layer0, ppl, :] lazy_select is replaced by data_loaders.ISRM_SR.gated_select gating the SR source axis by the DERIVED set emis_src_cells (Phase-2-core gated-provider deferral; see metadata.x_esd.phase2_pushdown_DRAFT). The sibling half \u2014 the src-cell rectangles as the [0:N_SRC] prefix of the full grid \u2014 is CLOSED by the `range` axis of the same per-axis vocabulary (esm-spec 8.9.2): src_W/src_S/src_E/src_N are declared `select` ranges over the SAME on-disk arrays as W/S/E/N.",
    "G3": "CLOSED (esm-spec 8.9). FF10/zip semantics ARE expressible now: EGU_Emis declares `reader_options` (the *egu* member glob + the asserted header row), a `codes` map on `pollutant` (POLID text -> the pathway enum, an unrecognised code DROPS the record) and a `record_filter` (a record with no coordinate or no annual total is not a record). The runner no longer reads, maps or filters this table.",
    "G5": "No polygon/choropleth plot type; best available is a centroid scatter (see examples).",
    "G6": "CLOSED (esm-spec 8.9.4). N_REC is still runtime-discovered (default 0), but the LOADER discovers it: EGU_Emis declares `extent: {metaparameter: N_REC}`, so prepare() samples it before it closes metaparameters and the surviving record count sizes emis_records. No caller counts rows. PUSHDOWN DRAFT: N_PPL is GONE \u2014 emis_src_cells is a derived index set whose extent is materialised from the emis_src_cells_faq producer (value-invention)."
   },
   "grid_mapping": {
    "grid_mapping_name": "lambert_conformal_conic",
    "standard_parallel": [
     33.0,
     45.0
    ],
    "latitude_of_projection_origin": 40.0,
    "longitude_of_central_meridian": -97.0,
    "earth_radius": 6370997.0,
    "false_easting": 0.0,
    "false_northing": 0.0
   }
  }
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "N_SRC": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 52411,
   "description": "ISRM source cells (first-52411 coarse subset of the InMAP grid)."
  },
  "N_RCV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 52411,
   "description": "ISRM receptor cells (== the source grid, same ordered cell set)."
  },
  "N_POP": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 596444,
   "description": "Full InMAP grid length of W/S/E/N/TotalPop/MortalityRate."
  },
  "N_LAYER": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 3,
   "description": "SR emission layers (only layer 0 is used)."
  },
  "N_REC": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 0,
   "description": "EGU FF10 point-source record count (runtime-discovered; G6)."
  }
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "src_cells": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_SRC"
  },
  "rcv_cells": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_RCV"
  },
  "pop_cells": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_POP"
  },
  "emis_layer": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_LAYER"
  },
  "pathways": {
   "kind": "categorical",
   "members": [
    "SOA",
    "pNO3",
    "pNH4",
    "pSO4",
    "PrimaryPM25"
   ]
  },
  "emis_records": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_REC"
  }
 },
 "data_loaders": {
  "ISRM_SR": {
   "kind": "static",
   "source": {
    "url_template": "s3://inmap-model/isrm_v1.2.1.zarr/"
   },
   "reference": {
    "url": "https://inmap.run/blog/2022/12/15/tutorial/",
    "notes": "InMAP ISRM v1.2.1 zarr store on the inmap-model S3 bucket."
   },
   "metadata": {
    "esio_format": "zarr",
    "tags": [
     "isrm",
     "source_receptor",
     "air_quality",
     "zarr",
     "health"
    ],
    "x_esd": {
     "format": "zarr",
     "zarr_format": 2,
     "consolidated": false,
     "sr_dim_order": [
      "emisLayer",
      "source",
      "receptor"
     ],
     "arrays": {
      "SOA": {
       "shape": [
        3,
        52411,
        52411
       ],
       "chunks": [
        1,
        100,
        52411
       ],
       "dtype": "<f4",
       "compressor": "blosc:lz4:clevel5:shuffle1",
       "fill": 0.0,
       "order": "C"
      },
      "pNO3": {
       "shape": [
        3,
        52411,
        52411
       ],
       "chunks": [
        1,
        100,
        52411
       ],
       "dtype": "<f4"
      },
      "pNH4": {
       "shape": [
        3,
        52411,
        52411
       ],
       "chunks": [
        1,
        100,
        52411
       ],
